This CMake support for Linux builds is adapted from the Windows CMake build
in contrib/windows-cmake/ for hwloc 2.15.

May be used with:
$ cmake [options] -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/path/to/install .
$ cmake --build .
$ cmake --build . --target INSTALL

The "Debug" build type is also available, it enables lots of
verbose debug messages and assertions.

Options:
-DHWLOC_SKIP_LSTOPO=1 to ignore lstopo
-DHWLOC_SKIP_TOOLS=1 to ignore other hwloc command-line tools
-DHWLOC_SKIP_INCLUDES=1 to ignore header installation
-DHWLOC_WITH_LIBXML2=ON to use libxml2 instead of minimal XML
-DHWLOC_WITH_OPENCL=ON to enable OpenCL support
-DHWLOC_WITH_CUDA=ON to enable CUDA support (requires CMake 3.17+)
-DHWLOC_ENABLE_PLUGINS=ON to enable plugin support (requires BUILD_SHARED_LIBS=ON)
-DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS=ON to build shared libraries (default is OFF for static)

This build enables the Linux backend and automatically detects optional
dependencies such as:
- libnuma (for NUMA support)
- libudev (for device enumeration)
- libpciaccess (for PCI device support)
- libxml2 (for full XML support)
- OpenCL
- CUDA

Note: hwloc 2.15 uses autotools by default. This CMake build is a community
port and may not have all features of the autotools build.